  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Hasam Nikhu Alias Neku Kha vs The State Of Maharashtra on 6 April, 2023 Author: Anuja Prabhudessai Bench: Anuja Prabhudessai 2023:Bhc-As:10637 P.H. Jayani 27(A) Aba3233.2 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 3233 Of 2022 Hasam Nikhu alias Neku Kha ... Appl v/s. The State of Maharashtra .... Res Mr. Veerdhaval Kakade for the Applicant. Mr. S.V. Gavand, App for the State. Coram: Smt. Anuja Prabhudessai, J. Dated : 06th April, 2023. P. C. :- .",
    "facts": "3. It is the case of the prosecution that on 25/09/2022, the vehicle bearing No.R.J.19, GC-8007 was intercepted and gutkha, pan masala P.H. Jayani 27(A) ABA3233.2022.doc and scented tobacco which are prohibited items, were seized from the said vehicle. The vehicle is owned by the Applicant and hence, crime came to be registered against the Applicant for committing the aforesaid offences. Subsequently, by order dated 09/03/2023, this Court had directed the Applicant to join the investigation. Learned APP states that pursuant to the said order, the Applicant has Hasam Nikhu Alias Neku Kha vs The State Of Maharashtra on 6 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/38595516/ 1 reported to the Investigating Officer and that he has been investigated. Learned APP, under instructions, states that the presence of the Applicant is not required for the purpose of custodial interrogation.",
